# ADR 0023 · UX-SPEC §5.1 — a new user starts work on a task with the pointer alone: the only
# keyboard input is the card's title, typed into the field the column's `+` focused.
#
# Board → Todo's `+` → New card → the card's ⋯ → Create worktree → pick the repository → the
# card's ⋯ → Open worktree → the tab strip's `+` → Terminal → `← Worktrees`. The card menu's
# items are numbered over what the card can do (TESTING-HARNESS §3): on a local board a fresh
# card lists the seven pickers (0–6), then Create worktree (7); once it links a worktree, Open
# worktree follows at 8. The workspace itself is not photographed: an empty terminal over the
# session's translucent window rule does not clear the virtual lane's capture guard.
#
# Virtual-lane only: it takes shots.
fixture: board
await idle 20000
assert screen == Hub && hub_tab == Worktrees && overlay absent

# The title bar's section nav: Board.
click hub.tab[2]
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert lists.board.rows[1].label == "Todo" && lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "2"

# Todo's `+` opens New card on Todo; its title takes the keyboard, and the footer's Create files it.
click board.column[1].add
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await idle 10000
assert dialog.name == CardCreate && dialog.fields[0].focused == true
type Wire the pointer journeys
assert dialog.fields[0].value == "Wire the pointer journeys"
click dialog.button[2]
await overlay absent 10000
await lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "3" 10000
await lists["board.cards"].selected.label == "Wire the pointer journeys" 10000
assert focused == "board.column[1].card[2]"
shot card-created

# The card's ⋯ → Create worktree asks which repository; a click on acme/api creates it, and the
# card moves to In Progress with it.
move board.column[1].card[2]
click board.column[1].card[2].menu
await targets["menu.item[7]"] exists 5000
shot card-menu
click menu.item[7]
await dialog.name == CardPicker 10000
await targets["dialog.row[1]"] exists 10000
click dialog.row[1]
await overlay absent 10000
await lists.board.selected.label == "In Progress" 30000
await lists["board.cards"].selected.label == "Wire the pointer journeys" 10000
await idle 30000
assert lists.board.rows[1].badges[0] == "2" && lists.board.rows[2].badges[0] == "2"
shot card-has-worktree

# The same card's ⋯ now offers Open worktree (item 8), which opens its workspace.
click board.column[2].card[1].menu
await targets["menu.item[8]"] exists 5000
click menu.item[8]
await screen == Workspace 20000
await lists.tabs.rows[2] exists 20000
assert lists.tabs.rows[0].label ~= "flt-6-wire-the-pointer-journeys"
assert targets["workspace.back"] exists && targets["tabs.new"] exists

# The strip's `+` → Terminal opens a fourth tab and selects it.
click tabs.new
await targets["menu.item[0]"] exists 5000
click menu.item[0]
await lists.tabs.rows[3] exists 20000
await focused == tabs.tab[3] 20000

# `← Worktrees` returns to the Hub, where the new worktree is listed and still running, and the
# cursor is on it: back lands on the worktree just left even though the board opened it.
click workspace.back
await screen == Hub 10000
assert overlay absent
await lists.worktrees.rows[0].id == "acme/api#flt-6-wire-the-pointer-journeys" 10000
await lists.worktrees.selected.id == "acme/api#flt-6-wire-the-pointer-journeys" 10000
dump back-in-hub
quit
